1 HELP
    govax a VAX software emulator.  It supports execution of a subset
    of the VAX instruction set.  It also contains emulation of VAX hardware,
    memory management, and console functions.  The console functions are
    extended beyond existing VAX implementation to include an assembler
    and a debugger, modeled on the VMS debugger, with breakpoints,
    stepping, and commands to examine and change the machine.

    You can get help on a topic by using the HELP command, followed by
    one or more keywords.  For example, to get help on the SHOW command,
    issue the command:

           HELP SHOW

    To get help on the SHOW LOGICAL subcommand to SHOW, use the command:

           HELP SHOW LOGICAL



    For additional information, see the help on the following command topics:

    @               Run a command procedure (a file of DCL commands)
    ANALYZE         Describe object and image files, as VMS's ANALYZE does
    ASSIGN          Create a logical name (equivalence first)
    BACKUP          List, restore, compare, or save VMS BACKUP save sets
    CALL            Run a command procedure's subroutine at a new level
    CLEAR           Clear memory, symbols, strings
    COPY            Copy a file between the host and a mounted volume
    CREATE          Create a directory or a logical name table
    DEASSIGN        Delete a logical name
    DEFINE          Create a logical name
    DELETE          Delete a file on a mounted volume
    DIRECTORY       List the files on a mounted volume
    DEBUG           Start the debugger on the virtual VAX
    DISMOUNT        Detach a device's mounted disk-image container
    DECK            Mark data lines that start with "$" (EOD ends them)
    CONTINUE        Do nothing (ON ERROR THEN CONTINUE)
    EDIT            Edit a file with an editor on the host
    EOD             End a command procedure's data lines
    EXIT            End a command procedure, or govax at the terminal
    FORTRAN         Compile a FORTRAN source file into a MACRO-32 source file
    IF              Run a command when an expression is true
    GOSUB           Call a subroutine at a label (RETURN comes back)
    GOTO            Go on at a label of a command procedure
    INITIALIZE      Initialize the virtual VAX, or a disk-image container
    LIBRARY         Create, change, or list a macro, object, or text library
    LINK            Link object modules into an executable image
    LOAD            Load a saved memory image
    MACRO           Assemble a MACRO-32 source file into an object module
    MOUNT           Attach a disk-image container file to a device
    ON              Choose what a command procedure does when a command fails
    PRINT           Print messages or expressions
    PURGE           Delete old versions of files on a mounted volume
    QUIT            Quit govax
    RENAME          Rename or move files on a mounted volume
    RUN             Load and run a VAX/VMS image
    SAVE            Save the machine state
    SET             Set the state of the console
    SHOW            Display the state of the console
    STOP            Delete a process
    TEST            Run the emulator's debugging sequences
    TIME            Run a command and report how long it took
    TYPE            Display a file on a mounted volume or the host
    VMINIT          Initialize a VM map
    ZERO            Clear the virtual VAX's memory

    The commands that examine and control the machine itself (EXAMINE,
    DEPOSIT, STEP, breakpoints, the registers) are the debugger's; type
    DEBUG for its prompt, DBG>, and HELP there for its commands.

    Other topics:

    ABOUT           About govax
    CONFIG          govax's configuration settings, and how to set them
    KEYS            The control keys: Ctrl/C, Ctrl/Y, and Ctrl/Z
    PSL             The processor status longword and its fields
    STARTUP         What govax does as it starts: the system volume,
                    STARTUP.COM, and SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM
    XFC             govax's extended function codes
